# Everything listed here is excluded from the "build context" — the set of
# files Docker uploads to the build engine before running the Dockerfile.
#
# This matters for two reasons:
#   1. Speed. node_modules here is ~500MB; sending it on every build is wasted
#      time, and the Dockerfile reinstalls dependencies anyway.
#   2. Safety. Without the .env line below, your real secrets would be copied
#      into the image by `COPY . .` and anyone who pulls the image could read
#      them with `docker history`. This is the single most common way secrets
#      leak out of a container.

# dependencies (reinstalled inside the image from package-lock.json)
node_modules
.pnp
.pnp.js

# build output (regenerated by `next build` inside the image)
.next
out
build
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# secrets — never allow these into an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# editor and OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.log

# docs and deployment files (not needed to build the app)
README.md
LICENSE
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
